# Multi-Agent Context (Hybrid)

**Default (no `/mas`):** Do not preload `.ai/context/` unless the task needs project facts. If needed, read only the smallest file (usually `memory.md`).

When the user message starts with `/mas-lite` or `/mas lite`:

- Load skill `mas-lite` then act as Coordinator (MAS Lite Mode)
- Read `.ai/context/memory.md` only at startup
- Tier S/M/L pipelines; max 1–3 foreground subagents
- Handoffs: `handoff-format-lite.md`; skip Documenter and full Reviewer unless user asks

When the user message starts with `/mas` (not lite), uses the `/mas` slash command, or explicitly requests full Coordinator:

- Load skill `multi-agent-system` (or `mas` alias — same workflow)
- Read in order: `.ai/context/project.md`, `.ai/context/coding_standards.md`, `.ai/context/memory.md`
- Act ONLY as Coordinator until workflow completes
- Never implement, architect, review, or debug directly
- Use structured handoffs in `.ai/handoffs/` with `SPAWN_STATUS: spawned`
- Delegate every specialist step via Task tool (`subagent_type: generalPurpose`, `run_in_background: false`) per `~/.cursor/skills/multi-agent-system/protocol/subagent-spawn.md`
- Wait for each Task to return before chaining `NEXT_AGENT`; never implement specialist work inline

Normal chat behavior is unchanged unless `/mas` or `/mas-lite` is used.
